---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Inspiration"
  category="About | Design Philosophy"
  year=""
  description="Sources of inspiration shaping Florian Froment's approach to engineering, design and innovation."
>

  <p slot="intro" class="hero-intro">
    My approach to engineering is shaped by the intersection
    of technology, industrial design, architecture and nature.
    I am particularly interested in systems where function
    naturally creates form.
  </p>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      01 | Swiss Design
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Clarity before decoration.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Swiss Design strongly influences the way I organise information
        and communicate technical ideas.
      </p>

      <p>
        Grid systems, typography, hierarchy and intentional use of
        empty space create interfaces where complexity remains readable.
      </p>

      <p>
        I apply the same principle to engineering |
        structure first, then refinement.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      02 | Apple
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Technology made understandable.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I am inspired by the way Apple presents complex technologies
        through simple interactions, restrained visual language
        and strong product storytelling.
      </p>

      <p>
        The product remains the central element |
        the interface exists primarily to reveal how it works,
        why it matters and how it feels to use.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      03 | Biomimicry
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Nature as an engineering reference.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Biological systems provide highly optimised solutions
        to problems involving movement, weight, adaptability
        and energy efficiency.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am particularly interested in translating these principles
        into robotics and mechanical architectures |
        not by copying nature directly, but by understanding
        the logic behind its solutions.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      04 | Industrial Machines
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Mechanical systems as architecture.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Large machines, robotics and manufacturing systems
        are a constant source of inspiration.
      </p>

      <p>
        Their structure exposes the direct relationship
        between forces, motion, materials and geometry.
      </p>

      <p>
        I especially appreciate machines where the mechanical
        architecture remains visually understandable |
        where each component appears to have a clear purpose.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      05 | Materials
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Let materials express themselves.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I am interested in the visual and mechanical qualities
        of materials such as titanium, aluminium, carbon fibre,
        steel and brass.
      </p>

      <p>
        Surface treatments, machining marks and raw finishes
        can become part of the identity of an object rather than
        elements that must always be hidden.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      06 | Architecture
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Structure as visual language.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Architecture influences the way I think about proportion,
        mass, repetition and structural logic.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am particularly drawn to projects where materials
        and construction techniques remain visible and become
        part of the aesthetic itself.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      07 | Exploration
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Inspiration comes from connecting fields.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Many of my ideas emerge from combining concepts
        that initially belong to different disciplines |
        mechanical engineering, robotics, visualisation,
        architecture, software and industrial design.
      </p>

      <p>
        I see innovation less as inventing from nothing
        and more as creating new connections between
        existing principles.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

</ProjectLayout>